<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Askia Muhammad</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/1493">1493</a>–<a href="/years/1528">1528</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Askia al-Hajj Muhammad, Muhammad Toure, Askia Muhammad I</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Askia Muhammad, also known as Askia al-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hajj">Hajj</a> Muhammad or Muhammad Toure, was the ruler who seized power in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/songhai-empire">Songhai Empire</a> in 1493 and founded the Askia dynasty. He expanded the empire, organised its administration and army, and promoted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> and scholarship. His pilgrimage to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a> strengthened his legitimacy as a Muslim ruler.</p></div>
